# NER Evaluation with Experiment Tracking

This example shows how to use `neo4j_experiment_tracker` for tracking your NER evaluation experiments.

## Setup

```bash
# Create virtual environment
cd /Users/amir.layeghneo4j.com/ner-eval
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies (from local experiment_tracker)
pip install -e /Users/amir.layeghneo4j.com/genai-cloud/experiment_tracker

# Or using uv
uv venv
source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install -e /Users/amir.layeghneo4j.com/genai-cloud/experiment_tracker
```

## Run the Example

```bash
python experiment_example.py
```

## Tracker Types

| Type | Use Case | Backend |
|------|----------|---------|
| `none` | Local development, testing | Console logging only |
| `vertex` | Production on GCP | Google Vertex AI Experiments |
| `auto` | Auto-detect from environment | Depends on `WORKFLOW_PLATFORM` |

## Key Concepts

### 1. Creating a Tracker

```python
from neo4j_experiment_tracker import create_tracker, TrackerType

tracker = create_tracker(
    tracker_type=TrackerType.NONE,  # "none", "vertex", or "auto"
    experiment_name="my-experiment",
    run_id="run-001",
    tags={"team": "ml"},
)
```

### 2. Using Context Manager (Recommended)

```python
with tracker:
    tracker.log_params({"learning_rate": 0.001})
    tracker.log_metrics({"accuracy": 0.95})
    tracker.log_artifact("/path/to/results.json", artifact_type="results")
```

### 3. Logging Methods

| Method | Purpose | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| `log_params()` | Hyperparameters, config | `{"batch_size": 32}` |
| `log_metrics()` | Numeric metrics | `{"f1_score": 0.85}` |
| `log_artifact()` | Files, models | `"/path/to/model.pkl"` |
| `set_tags()` | Labels, categories | `{"status": "completed"}` |

### 4. Step-wise Metrics

```python
for epoch in range(10):
    # Train...
    tracker.log_metrics({"loss": 0.5 - epoch * 0.04}, step=epoch)
```

## Switching to Vertex AI (Production)

When deploying to GCP:

```python
tracker = create_tracker(
    tracker_type="vertex",
    experiment_name="ner-evaluation",
    run_id="prod-run-001",
    project_id="your-gcp-project",
    location="europe-west1",
)
```

Or set environment variables:
```bash
export WORKFLOW_PLATFORM=gcp
export WORKFLOW_GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-gcp-project
export WORKFLOW_GCP_REGION=europe-west1
export EXPERIMENT_TRACKER=auto  # Will auto-detect vertex
```
